    {
     "type": "concept",
     "title": "A Second Body of Health Privacy Law Now Exists",
     "content": "Step back and see what has happened.\n\nFor most of your profession's history, health privacy had one center of gravity. If you knew HIPAA, you knew the rules. A second body of law now sits beside it, built on a different premise and enforced by different people.\n\nHold on to four things:\n\n• **Coverage is defined by meaning, not by source.** These statutes ask what the data reveals about health status, and they count inferences. That is why data your organization never called health data is now regulated health data\n• **The private right of action is the engine.** It converts a compliance topic into a litigation topic, and litigation topics get funded. Expect this to keep shaping behavior faster than guidance does\n• **The HIPAA exemption is data-shaped.** No health system is exempt as an entity. The only honest answer to \"does this apply to us?\" is an inventory\n• **The law is moving.** States keep enacting and amending; scope and enforcement questions are live in the courts. Learn structures, verify current text, and never advise on statutory application yourself — that belongs to counsel and your privacy officer\n\nWhat HIM contributes is the thing nobody else in the building can produce: an accurate, defensible account of what data exists, where it came from, and where it goes.\n\nFrom here the book moves from what these laws say to how the data actually escapes — the pixels, the SDKs, the vendor contracts, and the federal regulators watching all of it.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"55\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"34\">FOUR THINGS TO CARRY FORWARD</text><rect x=\"50\" y=\"100\" width=\"490\" height=\"290\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(139,92,246,0.12)\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"295\" y=\"150\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"21\">MEANING, NOT SOURCE</text><text x=\"295\" y=\"204\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"18\">Coverage turns on what the</text><text x=\"295\" y=\"242\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"18\">data reveals about health</text><text x=\"295\" y=\"280\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"18\">status — inferences count</text><text x=\"295\" y=\"340\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"17\">The opposite of HIPAA's test</text><rect x=\"560\" y=\"100\" width=\"490\" height=\"290\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(239,68,68,0.12)\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"805\" y=\"150\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"21\">THE PRIVATE RIGHT OF ACTION</text><text x=\"805\" y=\"204\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"18\">Enforcement is no longer</text><text x=\"805\" y=\"242\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"18\">limited by regulator capacity</text><text x=\"805\" y=\"280\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"18\">Compliance becomes litigation</text><text x=\"805\" y=\"340\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"17\">Litigation topics get funded</text><rect x=\"50\" y=\"415\" width=\"490\" height=\"290\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.12)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"295\" y=\"465\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"21\">THE CARVE-OUT IS DATA-SHAPED</text><text x=\"295\" y=\"519\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"18\">No health system is exempt</text><text x=\"295\" y=\"557\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"18\">as an entity — only its</text><text x=\"295\" y=\"595\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"18\">HIPAA-regulated data is</text><text x=\"295\" y=\"655\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"17\">The answer is an inventory</text><rect x=\"560\" y=\"415\" width=\"490\" height=\"290\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.12)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"805\" y=\"465\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"21\">THE LAW IS STILL MOVING</text><text x=\"805\" y=\"519\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"18\">States keep enacting and</text><text x=\"805\" y=\"557\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"18\">amending; scope questions</text><text x=\"805\" y=\"595\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"18\">are live in the courts</text><text x=\"805\" y=\"655\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"17\">Verify text before you act</text><rect x=\"50\" y=\"740\" width=\"1000\" height=\"130\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(20,184,166,0.12)\" stroke=\"#14b8a6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"790\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#14b8a6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"21\">WHAT HIM UNIQUELY CONTRIBUTES</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"836\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"19\">A defensible account of what data exists and where it goes</text><rect x=\"50\" y=\"900\" width=\"1000\" height=\"120\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(255,215,0,0.10)\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"948\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"20\">NEXT: HOW THE DATA ACTUALLY ESCAPES</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"988\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"19\">Pixels, SDKs, vendor contracts, and federal regulators</text></svg>",
      "caption": "Four durable takeaways, the contribution only HIM can make, and the bridge to the mechanics of data leakage."
     }
    }
